            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0210" n="128" xml:id="pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 437.00/11.</note>
                <head>[Extract.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-07-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 965.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 931, of the
                    16th ultimo, and to my telegram of the same date, I have the honor to report
                    that * * * the Governments of France, Germany, and Great Britain have now
                    formally proposed that this question be submitted to arbitration, and have
                    requested the Cuban Government to suggest a tribunal or person before whom the
                    case can be heard.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
